# Operator acceptance gates

- Replace all example identities/digests and review subscription/region, names,
  VNet overlap, provider registration, capacity, paid SKUs and platform TLS policy.
- Verify existing input vault and new target vault governance, scoped grants,
  secret rotation, purge protection and distinct PostgreSQL role passwords.
- Build and approve immutable images with the operator's container/PostgreSQL
  host policy and verified snapshot or deliberately empty evidence.
- Review MANIFEST.md, RULES.md, GITHUB-APPS.md and AGENT-MCP.md. MCP stays off.
- Validate Bicep and independently review what-if; generation is not apply.
- Deploy infrastructure with runtimeEnabled false, then wait for successful
  exact provisioning and ingestion executions before enabling the app.
- Confirm HTTPS/OAuth, trusted proxy peers and spoof rejection, private verified
  PostgreSQL TLS, image digests, readiness, logs, retention and restore.
- Explicitly accept single-replica/database failure domains and the unencrypted
  private ingress-to-container hop, or design a separately reviewed alternative.

No checkbox is completed by static validation. Missing evidence remains unknown.
